      "id": "ICI-01",
      "title": "The additive index of the trace-zero corner",
      "anchor": "lifts-inert-index",
      "statement": "For a discretely valued field with unramified involution, uniformizer ϖ fixed by σ, residue cardinal q² and some integral x with Δ=σ(x)−x a unit, put T={u∈𝒪:σ(u)=−u}. For every f≥0, [ϖ^{−f}T:T]=q^f. After an admissible row representative and a lift are fixed, its possible corrected corners modulo integral changes form a translate of this quotient.",
