      "status": "independently reviewed",
      "correspondence": "The actual call in the AbelianVarietyTheory inert integral supplies this index alongside the elementary-divisor row index. The two explicit inverse additive maps commute with ϖ, giving [T:ϖT]^2=q². Injective scaling identifies each successive quotient with T/ϖT.",
      "review": "A second reader checked both directions of the two-coordinate calculation, the sign conventions and descent modulo ϖ against the pinned supplier."
    },
    {
      "id": "ICI-02",
      "title": "A trace-zero corner in residue characteristic two",
      "anchor": "lifts-inert-index-example",
      "statement": "For L=ℚ₂(ω) with ω²+ω+1=0, σ(ω)=−1−ω and ϖ=2, the integral trace-zero subgroup is ℤ₂η, η=1+2ω a unit. At zero row and f=2 the corrected corners modulo T have precisely the four representatives 0,η/4,η/2,3η/4.",
